WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:40.820
[Music]

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.900
[Lynn Corwin:] I, I had a lovely time, Hal.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.220
[Hal Grover:] Yeah, sure. I'm glad you did.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:52.520
You're, you're all right. Oh look, it's late.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.660
[Lynn Corwin:] Will I see you tomorrow?

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.880
[Hal Grover:] No, not tomorrow.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:01.920
Some of us fellows are going to the drag races
over the weekend.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.720
But I'll call you sometime when I get back.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.060
[Lynn Corwin:] Fine. I'll be waiting.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.320
[Hal Grover:] Well, I'll be seeing you.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:43.280
[Music]

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.980
[Mrs. Corwin:] Lynn?

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.940
[Lynn Corwin:] Yes, Mother?

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.200
[Mrs. Corwin:] Oh, I guess I must have dozed
off.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.140
I was just going to rest my eyes for a minute.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.660
What time is it?

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:59.140
[Lynn Corwin:] Oh, it's just a little after
11:00.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.920
[Mrs. Corwin:] You're home early.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.520
Everything go all right?

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.240
[Lynn Corwin:] Oh, perfect!

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.260
I still can't believe it.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:09.220
Mom, he took me to the country club.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:13.940
Imagine me, dancing at the country club with
Hal Grover.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.840
I, I wish you could have been there, Mom.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.160
They even had a combo.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.600
Thanks, Mom.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.920
Thanks for making me this dress.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:34.520
I know you should have spent the time sewing
for your customers,

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:37.300
but the dress was exactly right.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.720
I didn't feel a bit out of place.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.540
[Mrs. Corwin:] Well, when I sew for Hal's
mother and her friends,

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.240
I see the kind of dresses they wear, and I
just --

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.220
[Lynn Corwin:] I know Hal was impressed.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.420
And I think that's why he took me to the country
club.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.340
He wanted to show me off.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.360
He likes me, Mother.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.260
I just know he likes me a lot.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:59.540
[Mrs. Corwin:] Well then dear, what the dress cost was worth it.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.180
[Music]

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.600
[Narrator:] Unfortunately, the final cost
of the dress

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.560
has not been calculated.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:09.940
The price that Lynn Corwin must pay will be
a high one.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:16.220
[Mrs. Corwin:] Going up to bed now, dear?
[Inaudible].

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:19.600
[Music]

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.200
[Narrator:] The dress, like many other things
in today's world,

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:28.020
is part of an enormous subtle pressure which
our times put upon young people.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.439
Evidence of the pressure is plentiful almost
anywhere you go.

00:03:33.439 --> 00:03:35.819
Evidence of the worship of sex appeal,

00:03:35.819 --> 00:03:39.259
as if it were the final essence of personality.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:58.960
[Drumming and music]

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:02.560
Who is to blame if young people respond to
this pressure,

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.760
reenacting in the privacy of parked cars

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:07.040
a theme hurled at them from every side?

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.140
Who is to blame if they respond to what

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:13.280
an anxiety-ridden world seems to be telling
them?

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.280
"Dance faster, little children."

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:24.840
[Music and singing]

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.380
The lyrics in the shadowy room may be suggestive.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.740
But at that they suggest something more human

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.920
than most of the headlines around the spinning
globe.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:55.840
[Music and singing]

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:00.680
Faster. Faster. Faster. Faster! Race to live
while you may.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:04.780
[Music]

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.340
And a part of the frenzy to experience,

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.200
to learn about everything,

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.560
takes Hal Grover and his friends to another
part of the state

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:15.200
to participate in the weekend meeting of drag
racers

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.280
from all over the area.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:25.220
[Music and sounds of car engines and tires]

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:30.200
But drag racing is not the only amusement
a city has to offer.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:06:19.420
[Music and singing]

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:25.200
[Hal's friend:] Ah, how much longer are they
gonna be?

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.580
You'd think Hal could find some other place
besides our room.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.480
Man, I'm tired.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.000
I want to go to bed.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:35.240
[Hal's other friend:] Hal and his women.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:37.720
Oh, finally!

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:41.880
[Friend:] Yeah. Hey, check that out.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:44.260
Come on, give up lady.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:47.740
[Other friend:] Still? He never quits.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:56.360
[Music and singing]

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.940
[Friend:] Well, don't you even have to take
her back where you found her?

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.700
[Hal Grover:] Ah, she doesn't live far.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:03.140
Besides, she has to go home alone.

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:05.100
Her parents are the strict kind.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.240
They don't allow her to go out with boys.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:09.160
[Laughter]

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:13.420
[Other friend:] So she can go home and tell
them about meeting a new girlfriend...Hally?

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:16.040
[Laughter]

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:26.140
[Music and singing]

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:29.140
[Dr. Jamison:] When I turned up the third
case

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:31.260
of primary syphilis in ten days,

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.820
I knew Oakdale was up against it.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:38.020
I don't mind saying I was amazed.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:43.200
I've been out of medical school for 15 years,

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.580
and haven't seen a handful of cases.

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:50.480
And now, three of them in ten days.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:53.620
And I'm not the only doctor in town reporting
cases.

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:57.020
It looks like a real outbreak.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:58.960
[Man at desk:] Well, that's for sure.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:02.160
And from the reports you and the other doctors
have sent us,

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:07.380
one that's pretty well confined to kids from
12 to 19 years old.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:12.020
What's more, it's too big for a health department
this size

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:13.580
to handle on our own.

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.740
That's one reason we've asked for assistance

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:17.920
from the state health department.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.560
They're sending us John Camp,

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.860
who is especially trained for this work.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:25.380
Mrs. Elliott has been interviewing the patients

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:27.050
you and the other doctors have sent us.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:28.850
But she can only do so much.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:31.740
A public health nurse has a lot of other duties.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:35.620
[John Camp:] Hello.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:38.500
[Man at desk:] Well hi, John. We were just talking about you.

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:40.680
You know Mrs. Elliott.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:44.360
This is Dr. Jamison, President of the County
Medical Society.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.090
Doctor, this is John Camp.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:49.080
He's field representative from the venereal
disease program.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.180
[Dr. Jamison:] Mr. Camp, we have a lot of
work to do.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:09:01.180
[Narrator:] Every doctor in Oakdale has a
lot of work to do, including Dr. Sam Holdeen.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:05.040
Dr. Sam, to those patients who have known
him for many years.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:08.850
[Miss Day:] Won't you step in, Lynn.

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:10.640
[Dr. Sam Holdeen:] Why, hello, Lynn.

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:11.640
I'm glad to see you.

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:13.700
Since we got you through the tonsillitis stage,

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.480
I haven't had much chance to keep acquainted.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:18.260
[Lynn Corwin:] Oh, I don't think I'm really
sick now, Dr. Sam.

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:21.760
But this stuff is a nuisance, and I'd just
as soon be rid of it.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.380
[Dr. Sam Holdeen:] All right, let's find out about this stuff.

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:26.900
[Lynn Corwin:] Well, it's a breaking-out.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.820
I tried to hide it with makeup,

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:31.380
but it's all over me.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.740
Mother thought it might be the three-day measles,

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:35.430
but I may have had them.

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:37.200
[Dr. Sam Holdeen:] Well, let me call the nurse.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.500
and we'll check you over.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.640
Miss Day, would you come in, please?

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:46.300
[Lynn Corwin:] Thanks a lot, Edna.

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:51.240
Well, Dr. Sam, what do you think it is?

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:54.519
[Dr. Sam Holdeen:] Could be a number of things.

00:09:54.519 --> 00:09:56.999
Maybe an allergy to some food.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.440
I'm writing you a prescription that may help.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:04.220
You use this for a couple of days,

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:06.400
and let me know if there's no change.

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:08.420
[Lynn Corwin:] Okay, I will.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:09.560
I feel better already,

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:11.520
now that there's something I can do about
it.

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:15.660
Well, bye.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:18.720
[Dr. Sam Holdeen:] Oh goodbye, Lynn.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.400
Give my regards to your mother.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:33.460
[Music]

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:35.740
It could be an allergic reaction.

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:38.860
That rash isn't entirely atypical.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.620
[Narrator:] It looks like syphilis.

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:44.960
[Dr. Sam]: Lynn Corwin?

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:46.460
It couldn't be!

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:48.420
[Narrator:] Now hold on, Sam.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.040
You're a doctor.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:52.780
You know VD doesn't play favorites.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:55.200
Just because you brought that girl into the
world

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.940
and have taken care of her all of her life

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:59.120
doesn't make her immune.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.860
Why didn't you take a blood test?

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:05.140
[Dr. Sam:] Because it just couldn't be!

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:09.980
[Narrator:] As doctors are human,

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.820
so there may be in their hearts the wish

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:14.540
that some things just couldn't be.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:17.340
But as doctors are men of science,

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:21.060
dedicated to the welfare of all their fellow
beings,

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:24.080
that wish must give way to a review of the
facts.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:28.340
And the facts leave no room for wishful thinking.

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:30.640
In the long years of his practice,

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:33.519
Dr. Sam has too often seen the final tragedy

00:11:33.519 --> 00:11:35.939
of latent untreated syphilis.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.780
He has seen those whose minds were destroyed,

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:42.120
whose bodies were horribly crippled.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:46.520
And he has seen helpless babies born of syphilitic
mothers,

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:48.920
the most tragic victims of all.

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:52.820
What Dr. Sam knows only too well

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:56.000
wipes out every trace of his momentary wish
that

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:59.940
such things couldn't be, where Lynn Corwin
is concerned.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:02.240
Especially with Lynn Corwin,

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:06.280
one of his children, such things must not
be.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:11.220
Syphilis can be cured, and if, regrettably,

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:15.180
Lynn has syphilis, she must be cured.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:21.240
[Dr. Sam Holdeen:] Lynn, this is Dr. Sam.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:22.400
I think maybe you better...

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:25.860
[Narrator:] As Lynn Corwin makes an appointment
with Dr. Sam,

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:28.300
other doctors have sent in young people whose
disease

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:30.160
has already been diagnosed.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:34.600
Appointments with John Camp, the field representative.

00:12:36.260 --> 00:12:38.940
John Camp's job is not an easy one.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:42.320
Nobody wants to hear what he must tell those
he interviews.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:46.760
And nobody wants to tell him what he must
find out.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:49.980
For syphilis can be halted only if everyone
involved

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.980
is located and examined.

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.220
With the approval of their personal physicians,

00:12:57.220 --> 00:13:01.180
John Camp interviews every patient diagnosed
as having syphilis,

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:02.980
to learn the names of all those

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:05.500
with whom the patient has had sexual intercourse.

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:09.920
[John Camp:] I appreciate your bringing your
daughter down, Mr. Nedrick.

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:11.499
The interview is confidential though,

00:13:11.499 --> 00:13:12.879
so if you'll just take a seat in the hall.

00:13:12.879 --> 00:13:15.219
[Mr. Nedrick:] Yeah, I'll have a seat in the
hall.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:17.779
I just brought her in to see if you could
get it out of her.

00:13:17.779 --> 00:13:20.680
I can't find out what kind of trash she's
been running with.

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:22.440
[John Camp:] Please take a seat in the hall,
Mr. Nedrick.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:25.380
[Mr. Nedrick:] Oh, I'm leaving. You're welcome
to her.

00:13:25.389 --> 00:13:27.489
She's no daughter of mine.

00:13:27.489 --> 00:13:32.840
[Music, and soft sobbing]

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:36.720
[Narrator:] The parents of teenagers who have
blundered blindly into infection

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:40.000
are sometimes more blind than the children
they condemn.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:44.360
John Camp is all too familiar with typical
parental reactions.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:49.460
[A mother:] It's that sex education they get
in the schools.

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:52.200
If my boy hadn't known about such filthy things,

00:13:52.209 --> 00:13:55.629
he wouldn't have got curious, and he wouldn't
be sick.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.280
I didn't want him to find out.

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:01.040
Not me nor his daddy told him nothing.

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:04.980
But some other busybodies did.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.300
[A father:] Oh, I'm surprised all right,

00:14:07.309 --> 00:14:09.409
but only that he had the guts to do it.

00:14:09.409 --> 00:14:11.740
He's the biggest pantywaist I ever saw.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:12.400
[Laughter]

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:16.760
But I sowed my wild oats when I was a boy but...

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:19.720
But I didn't think that kid of mine had it
in him.

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:21.040
[Laughter]

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:24.200
Hey look, I'm not gonna preach at him.

00:14:24.209 --> 00:14:26.509
It's the church's job to preach.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:29.940
[Woman sitting next to her husband:] My husband
and I will both tell you

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:32.140
it's not Junior's fault.

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:33.640
[A second mother:] It's all his fault.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.180
I just can't do a thing with him anymore.

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:38.000
[Music]

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:40.900
[Narrator:] Confronted with those who have
been judged,

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:43.680
who come to him even under the best of circumstances,

00:14:43.689 --> 00:14:45.889
ashamed and afraid,

00:14:45.889 --> 00:14:48.889
John Camp acts neither as judge nor prosecutor.

00:14:48.889 --> 00:14:52.000
He is an investigator dealing with the facts.

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:57.360
[John Camp:] No, you didn't get syphilis from
the toilet seat, Bill.

00:14:57.360 --> 00:15:00.320
You got it from sexual intercourse with somebody
who had it.

00:15:00.329 --> 00:15:03.469
Now, these are the people that we have to
talk about,

00:15:03.469 --> 00:15:05.700
for their protection as well as for yours.

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:07.860
[Narrator:] Nobody wants to talk.

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:10.700
But because John Camp sees beyond the patient

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:12.920
to the welfare of the whole community,

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:16.820
he must make these youngsters realize their
responsibility.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.800
[John Camp:] All right, Bill.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:25.480
Now, what about your very best girl?

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:30.480
[Bill:] She's, there isn't any--I haven't
got a best girl.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:32.880
[John Camp:] You wouldn't want to walk out
of this room

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:35.320
with somebody's life in your hands would you,
Bill?

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:38.420
[Bill:] I...No, but she's all right.

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:41.140
[John Camp:] Bill, that's something a doctor
has to decide.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.520
Now, her name is?

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.040
[Bill:] Her name's Betty.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:48.920
[Teen:] Her name is Mary.

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.720
[Teen 2:] His name is Jack.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:52.380
[Teen 3:] Her name is Susan.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:53.280
[Teen 4:] Roberta.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:54.120
[Teen 5:] Bob.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:55.040
[Teen 6:] JoAnn.

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:58.369
[Narrator:] The names are many, and there
is usually more than one,

00:15:58.369 --> 00:16:01.289
for the patient must tell the names of all
sexual contacts

00:16:01.289 --> 00:16:03.180
within the infectious period.

00:16:03.189 --> 00:16:05.800
if the chain of infection is to be broken.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.960
What makes John Camp's job more difficult,

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:11.480
and increases the danger to the community,

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:14.980
is the fact that there is sometimes no name
at all.

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:17.340
[John Camp:] All right, Tom, who else?

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:18.480
[Tom:] Nobody.

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:19.340
Just them.

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:21.580
Just them and some girl at the ballpark.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.739
I didn't even catch her name.

00:16:23.739 --> 00:16:25.159
[John Camp:] Where does she live?

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:26.820
[Tom:] Who knows, it was a night game.

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:28.100
We never got out of the park.

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:30.600
[John Camp:] Well, tell me what she looked
like,

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:32.259
anything you can remember about her.

00:16:32.259 --> 00:16:34.079
[Tom:] Oh, she was just a pickup.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:38.920
[John Camp:] She may be the reason you're
sitting where you are now.

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:43.420
[Tom:] If she is, I wish I'd never laid eyes
on her.

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:45.540
She really gave me the come-on,

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:47.360
and her a foot taller than me.

00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:52.560
Uh, she had sort of light blonde hair.

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:54.760
[Cheering]

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:57.660
[Narrator:] Starting with a known hangout,
the ballpark,

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:00.200
with only a vague description of a girl.

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:06.380
The field representative tries to find one
of the known contacts of an infected person,

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:09.440
and here, as with all other cases in Oakdale,

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:13.500
he is successful in locating a potential source
of syphilis,

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:16.300
the tall, aggressive blonde.

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:20.980
Unfortunately for other communities,

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:24.520
a number of contacts are named in surrounding
towns.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:28.560
Locating a possibly infected boyfriend in
Ashton may be simple.

00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:31.860
Since Ashton is across a state line,

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:36.280
another state health department is alerted,
to find the boyfriend.

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:43.360
Another field representative continues the search,

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:46.620
perhaps finding that in our increasingly mobile society,

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:49.560
a search has become more complicated.

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:56.900
The job of this field representative now becomes one

00:17:56.900 --> 00:18:00.020
of knocking on doors in the last known neighborhood.

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:01.980
Seeking clues.

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:03.640
Asking.

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:06.100
Continuing to ask.

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:09.580
Until he finds someone who knows where the
Farleys

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:10.880
or the Hagans

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:12.640
or the Smiths have moved.

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:14.880
To California.

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.940
To New Hampshire.

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:18.600
To Mexico.

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:21.740
The Oakdale outbreak has spread its tentacles
nationwide,

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:24.510
crossed an international boundary.

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:27.470
It is not and has not been from the beginning

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:29.110
Oakdale's problem alone.

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:32.980
Syphilis is not only an individual problem,

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:37.420
but a community problem as well, as Hal Grover's
father is finding out.

00:18:37.429 --> 00:18:40.309
[Ed Grover:] I always thought you were a good
doctor.

00:18:40.309 --> 00:18:43.220
But now I'm going to find out if there's any
legal action

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:44.340
that I can take.

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:48.000
It looks to me like you're violating medical
ethics.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:52.580
What a doctor treats a patient for is nobody
else's business.

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:56.540
But you had to call in the whole health department,

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:59.880
subjecting a boy to that kind of questioning.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:02.200
[Dr. Jamison:] Ed, those interviews are confidential.

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:05.280
If you know what the boy was asked, it's because
he told you.

00:19:05.289 --> 00:19:06.809
As for me,

00:19:06.809 --> 00:19:09.969
I was following good medical practice and
obeying the law.

00:19:09.969 --> 00:19:13.089
VD has to be reported to the health department.

00:19:13.089 --> 00:19:15.789
Protection of the public is more important

00:19:15.789 --> 00:19:18.580
than the temporary embarrassment to your boy.

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:20.500
[Ed Grover:] Him embarrassed?

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:23.400
His mother is sick with mortification,

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:26.640
and I can't stand to look my friends in the
eyes,

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.720
whether they know what's happened or not.

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:30.540
But he's not embarrassed.

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:36.060
I told him I didn't even want to claim him
for a son.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:38.300
You know what he said?

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:43.940
He looked at me as bold as brass,

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:50.720
and he said...you never did.

00:19:57.140 --> 00:20:02.140
I bought that boy everything in the world
he ever asked for.

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:04.820
Bicycles.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.400
Ponies.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:07.960
Car.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:11.800
He's got the best clothes...

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:15.640
and the biggest allowance in town.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:22.280
What more can he want?

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.780
[Dr. Jamison:] I don't know.

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:28.340
Maybe he wants the thing

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:31.080
he seems to have been looking for pretty desperately,

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:33.320
somebody who cares.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:40.380
[Mrs. Corwin:] I wasn't worried when she was
out with him.

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:43.680
He came from one of the best families in town.

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:46.420
[Mr. Corwin:] If it just wouldn't make it
harder for Lynn,

00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:48.460
I'd haul Hal Grover out in the town square

00:20:48.460 --> 00:20:50.500
and beat him within an inch of his life.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:53.780
[Dr. Sam Holdeen:] Well, that might be the
least of his troubles.

00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:55.360
I believe Lynn,

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:56.580
and I think you do, too.

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:58.700
When she says he was the only one.

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:01.660
[Lynn Corwin:] It isn't all Hal's fault.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:03.600
I could have...

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:06.840
Oh, if I'd just stopped to think.

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:09.340
But I wanted him to like me.

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:13.880
Mom said she wasn't worried when I was out
with him,

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:18.060
but I was the one she couldn't trust.

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:20.200
I was the one.

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:24.120
[Mrs. Corwin:] No. No, honey...

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:26.500
[Narrator:] Lynn is more fortunate than some,

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:30.000
to have parents who will make the difficult
effort to understand.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:35.920
With Dr. Sam's help, Lynn Corwin will be cured
of the physical disease,

00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:40.060
although she may never be free of its emotional
consequences.

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:47.120
The 50 or more young people who are victims
of the Oakdale outbreak

00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:48.700
will all be cured.

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:51.180
Either in the clinic of their health department

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:53.400
or by their personal physicians.

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:58.100
The outbreak in Oakdale will be over.

00:21:58.260 --> 00:22:02.320
The local health department's file marked closed.

00:22:03.180 --> 00:22:07.180
Somewhere, in a city where a drag race was held

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:08.960
is one who was forgotten.

00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:12.380
Whose name, if it was ever known, was not
reported.

00:22:13.400 --> 00:22:15.420
Is this your town?

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:17.860
Is this your daughter?

00:22:19.640 --> 00:22:21.380
Is this your son?

00:22:21.380 --> 00:22:27.280
[Music and singing]

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:29.580
Dance on, little children.

00:22:29.580 --> 00:22:43.660
[Music and singing]

